        "path": "Immunization.manufacturer",
        "comment": "CA Baseline Usage Notes: This is a reference to an organization that manufactures the vaccine. TBD: if there is a need to reference a 'DPD Company', a new extension should be created and used. A 'DPD Company' name, as used in the Health Canada DPF, indicates the organization (company) that holds the authorization to place the product on the market in Canada. This may not be the company that has manufactured the product, but it is the company that holds the legal responsibility for the use of the product in Canada and should be the same as the company named on the product label/packaging.",
